Subject: P7 revised - safe hardsub paths/publication and thumbnail probing without ffprobe

Base: current working tree after the revised P6, including the output-path, libass,
per-word yellow Kinetic, real video dimensions and thumbnail subtitle-offset fixes.
This is a patch artifact only; it has not been applied to the live source tree.

Changes:
- Use a unique work directory beside the destination and safe sub.srt/sub.ass filter names.
- Use absolute source/destination paths when FFmpeg runs in the work directory.
- Reject output paths pointing to the input video or SRT, including symlink aliases.
- Render to a staging video on the destination filesystem; rename only on success.
- Failure/empty output preserves the previous destination. RAII cleans only this job's work directory.
- Preserve libass checks, real video dimensions, yellow active words, punch accents and subtitle_offset_ms.
- Kinetic errors propagate; never silently fall back to full-sentence SRT.
- Generate temporary ASS through an explicit-path API; keep the existing .kinetic.ass wrapper.
- Probe thumbnail media with the existing PyAV dependency when ffprobe is absent.

Validation in an isolated source copy on macOS:
- Rust suite: 47 passed, excluding the unrelated keychain test.
- Real FFmpeg/libass integration tested both static and Kinetic captions with quoted/Unicode paths,
  subtitle offset before/after samples, failed rerenders, existing output preservation and cleanup.
- Python thumbnail suite: 7 passed, including no-ffprobe frame counts, cover boundary and delayed audio.
- cargo build --offline: passed without warnings after removing the test-only import from production.
- Patch applicability against the current tree is checked after generation.

The current SRT word timing remains estimated within each cue; P7 does not add audio forced alignment.

